BT /F1 11 Tf 72 720 Td (oxygenated and deoxygenated blood never mix. The wall of the left ventricle is much) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 705 Td (thicker than the wall of the right ventricle. This is because the left ventricle must) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 690 Td (pump blood all the way around the body, while the right ventricle only needs to pump) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 675 Td (blood a short distance to the lungs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 645 Td (The heart contains valves that keep blood flowing in one direction. The atrioventricular) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 630 Td (valves sit between each atrium and ventricle. On the right side this is the tricuspid) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 615 Td (valve and on the left side it is the bicuspid or mitral valve. The semilunar valves sit) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 600 Td (at the bases of the two main arteries leaving the heart. When a ventricle contracts, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 585 Td (pressure closes the atrioventricular valve, which prevents backflow into the atrium.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 570 Td (When the ventricle relaxes, the semilunar valve closes, which prevents blood flowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 555 Td (back from the artery. The closing of the valves causes the familiar lub-dub sound of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 540 Td (heartbeat.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 510 Td (The heart muscle itself needs a supply of oxygen. It is supplied by the coronary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 495 Td (arteries, which branch off the aorta and spread across the surface of the heart. If a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 480 Td (coronary artery becomes blocked, for example by a build-up of fatty material, part of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 465 Td (the heart muscle is starved of oxygen. This can cause a heart attack.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 435 Td (4. The route of blood through the heart) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 405 Td (Deoxygenated blood from the body returns to the heart through two large veins called the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 390 Td (venae cavae. It enters the right atrium. The right atrium contracts and pushes blood) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 375 Td (through the tricuspid valve into the right ventricle. The right ventricle then contracts) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 360 Td (and pumps the blood through a semilunar valve into the pulmonary artery, which carries) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 345 Td (it to the lungs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 315 Td (In the lungs, the blood is oxygenated and returns to the heart through the pulmonary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 300 Td (veins. It enters the left atrium, which contracts and pushes the blood through the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 285 Td (bicuspid valve into the left ventricle. The thick muscular left ventricle contracts) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 270 Td (strongly and pumps the blood through a semilunar valve into the aorta, the largest) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 255 Td (artery in the body. From the aorta, blood is carried to every organ except the lungs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 225 Td (A useful way to remember the order is: body, vena cava, right atrium, right ventricle,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 210 Td (pulmonary artery, lungs, pulmonary vein, left atrium, left ventricle, aorta, body.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 195 Td (Notice that the pulmonary artery is the only artery that carries deoxygenated blood, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 180 Td (the pulmonary vein is the only vein that carries oxygenated blood.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 150 Td (5. The cardiac cycle and heart rate) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 120 Td (The sequence of events in one heartbeat is called the cardiac cycle. It has three main) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 105 Td (stages. In atrial systole, the atria contract and push blood into the ventricles. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 90 Td (ventricular systole, the ventricles contract, the atrioventricular valves close, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 75 Td (blood is forced into the arteries. In diastole, the whole heart relaxes and the chambers) Tj ET
endstream
