BT /F1 11 Tf 72 720 Td (fill with blood again from the veins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 690 Td (The heartbeat is started by a small group of cells in the wall of the right atrium) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 675 Td (called the sinoatrial node, often called the pacemaker. It sends out regular electrical) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 660 Td (impulses that spread across the atria and make them contract. The impulse then reaches) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 645 Td (the atrioventricular node, which delays it slightly so that the atria finish emptying) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 630 Td (before the ventricles contract. The impulse then travels down special fibres in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 615 Td (septum and spreads up through the ventricle walls from the bottom, squeezing blood) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 600 Td (upwards into the arteries.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 570 Td (A resting adult heart beats about 60 to 80 times per minute. During exercise, the heart) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 555 Td (rate increases so that more oxygen and glucose reach the working muscles and more carbon) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 540 Td (dioxide is removed. Cardiac output is the volume of blood pumped by one ventricle per) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 525 Td (minute. It is calculated by multiplying the heart rate by the stroke volume, which is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 510 Td (the volume of blood pumped in one beat. Regular exercise strengthens the heart muscle,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 495 Td (increasing stroke volume, which is why trained athletes often have a low resting heart) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 480 Td (rate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 450 Td (6. Blood vessels) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 420 Td (There are three main types of blood vessel. Arteries carry blood away from the heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 405 Td (Because the blood in them is at high pressure, arteries have thick walls containing) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 390 Td (muscle and elastic fibres. The elastic fibres stretch as each surge of blood passes and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 375 Td (then recoil, which smooths out the flow. This surge can be felt as a pulse where an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 360 Td (artery passes close to the skin, such as at the wrist or neck.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 330 Td (Veins carry blood back towards the heart. The blood in veins is at low pressure, so) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 315 Td (veins have thinner walls and a wider lumen, which is the space inside the vessel. Veins) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 300 Td (contain valves that stop blood flowing backwards. Many veins run between skeletal) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 285 Td (muscles, and when these muscles contract they squeeze the veins and help push blood back) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 270 Td (towards the heart.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 240 Td (Capillaries are the smallest blood vessels. They connect arteries to veins and form) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 225 Td (dense networks called capillary beds in every tissue. The wall of a capillary is only) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 210 Td (one cell thick, which makes the diffusion distance very short. Oxygen and glucose) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 195 Td (diffuse out of the blood into the cells, and carbon dioxide and other wastes diffuse) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 180 Td (from the cells into the blood. Because there are so many capillaries, they provide a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 165 Td (huge surface area for exchange.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 135 Td (7. Blood) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 105 Td (Blood is made of a pale yellow liquid called plasma, in which several types of cell are) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 90 Td (suspended. Plasma is mostly water and carries dissolved substances such as glucose,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 75 Td (amino acids, carbon dioxide, urea, hormones and proteins. It also carries heat around) Tj ET
endstream
