BT /F1 11 Tf 72 720 Td (the body.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 690 Td (Red blood cells carry oxygen. They contain the red protein haemoglobin, which combines) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 675 Td (with oxygen in the lungs to form oxyhaemoglobin and releases it in the tissues. Red) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 660 Td (blood cells are adapted for their job: they have no nucleus, which leaves more room for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 645 Td (haemoglobin, and they have a biconcave disc shape, which gives them a large surface area) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 630 Td (for oxygen to diffuse in and out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 600 Td (White blood cells are part of the immune system. Some, called phagocytes, engulf and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 585 Td (digest pathogens. Others, called lymphocytes, produce antibodies that attach to specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 570 Td (pathogens and help destroy them. Platelets are small fragments of cells that help the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 555 Td (blood to clot at the site of a wound, which stops bleeding and prevents pathogens from) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 540 Td (entering the body.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 510 Td (8. Keeping the circulatory system healthy) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 480 Td (Coronary heart disease happens when fatty deposits build up in the walls of the coronary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 465 Td (arteries, narrowing them and reducing the flow of blood to the heart muscle. Risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 450 Td (factors include smoking, a diet high in saturated fat, high blood pressure, lack of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 435 Td (exercise, and a family history of heart disease. Some of these factors, such as diet,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 420 Td (smoking and exercise, can be changed by the choices a person makes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 390 Td (Treatments for heart disease include medicines called statins, which lower cholesterol) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 375 Td (in the blood, and stents, which are small mesh tubes inserted into a narrowed artery to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 360 Td (hold it open. In more serious cases a surgeon may perform a bypass operation, using a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 345 Td (section of blood vessel from elsewhere in the body to carry blood around the blocked) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 330 Td (part of the artery. Faulty heart valves can be replaced with mechanical valves or with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 315 Td (valves taken from animals.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 285 Td (Summary: the heart is a double pump with four chambers and one-way valves. It drives) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 270 Td (blood through arteries, capillaries and veins in two circuits, one to the lungs and one) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 255 Td (to the body. Blood carries oxygen in red blood cells, fights infection with white blood) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 240 Td (cells, clots with platelets, and transports dissolved substances in plasma.) Tj ET
